  @Description_f815267c89b8 = N'OpenAI''s speed-optimised image generation and editing model, released November 4, 2026 alongside GPT Image 2.6 Sunburst as the engine behind ChatGPT Images 2.6. Flare generates roughly 50% faster than GPT Image 2.5 (third-party measurement via its OpenRouter listing, which also reports a 400K context); Sunburst is the higher-detail sibling. Shares 2.6''s new capabilities: animated GIF output, SVG export, markup-guided edits, and a complexity parameter (defaults to high). Token-billed identically to Sunburst at $5/1M text input, $8/1M image input ($2/1M cached) and $30/1M image output. MJ never carried the 2.5 generation, so PriorVersionID points at GPT Image 2.'
